35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data shows a clear drop during the trial, but it reversed after.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system only logs named slots. Unplanned work is invisible to management.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The board minutes confirm the joint clinic failed because neither department owned the budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Agency cover is rising sharply. The therapy team is shrinking, but midwifery has slack.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The development budget is down by a quarter. Off-site visits generate no tariff revenue.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we justify a home follow-up program?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, that explains the joint clinic failure. We need clear ownership structures.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. The booking system gap means we cannot even measure the workload properly.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the midwifery slack is interesting. Could we leverage that for a new service?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, the budget cut means we must prioritize on-site services that bill at standard rates.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The shared nursing round lost a third of visits. Home visits are risky without support.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The car park fills by eleven. Any new outpatient service will face immediate capacity issues.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Data agreements take fourteen months. Any program relying on outside surgeries is too slow.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,The therapy staffing loss is severe. We cannot expand rehabilitation without new hires.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,On-site sessions bill at standard rates. We must focus on what we can deliver in-house.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The evidence suggests home-based programs are fragile without strong infrastructure.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We need a program that fits within existing physical and digital constraints.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Avoiding external dependencies is key. Internal coordination is more reliable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,Midwifery has capacity. A perinatal service could use existing staff effectively.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,A perinatal service on-site would generate revenue and use available staff. It seems viable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
